WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.818
Identify the form
Find the limit of two x cubed minus x, divided by x cubed plus four, as x
tends to positive infinity. Begin by identifying the form.

2
00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:28.273
An indeterminate form
Both the numerator and denominator tend to positive infinity. Direct
substitution therefore does not determine the result. We need to rewrite the
quotient.

3
00:00:28.273 --> 00:00:42.636
Divide numerator and denominator by x³
The highest power present is x cubed. Divide the entire numerator and
denominator by it, including every term, to preserve the value of the
quotient.

4
00:00:42.636 --> 00:00:55.636
Take the limit
One over x squared tends to zero, as does four over x cubed. The new
denominator tends to one, which is nonzero.

5
00:00:55.636 --> 00:01:10.000
Conclude
The result is two. We can check it because the degrees are equal and the ratio
of the leading coefficients is two divided by one.
